A decision tree is a machine-learning model that makes decisions through a sequence of questions. For example: Is the customer over 18? Has the payment failed before? Is the transaction unusually large? Decision trees are popular because they are easier to understand than many black-box models. They are often used in risk scoring, classification and business rules.

